// The Slug Menace - the Commorb v2, and Jorral who reads the door for you.
//
// THE ORB IS THE QUEST'S SPINE. Scan reads whatever is in front of you, Contact reaches Savant,
// and Playback repeats the last thing she said - which is the one of the three that matters,
// because the quest's instructions arrive by voice and a player who logs out mid-step has no
// other way to get them back. Wanted!'s orb had the same three verbs and this is the same shape.
//
// A SCAN IS NOT A DESTINATION. The orb never says where to go next: it confirms the thing the
// player is already standing in front of. That is why the Mayor's scan and the door's scan are
// the only two that do anything, and everything else gets "nothing worth reporting".

// =========================================================================== Scan
[opheld1,slug_commorb]
if (%slugmenace_stage = ^slugmenace_not_started) {
    ~mesbox("The orb lights up and stays blank. There is nothing it has been asked to look for.");
    return;
}
// The Mayor, from anywhere in the room with him. This is the reading Savant asks for in his own
// conversation and the one Col. O'Niall will not take a report without.
if (%slugmenace_stage = ^slugmenace_asking & %slugmenace_met_hobb = ^slugmenace_on
        & %slugmenace_door_scanned = ^slugmenace_off) {
    if (~slugmenace_near_hobb = true) {
        @slugmenace_scan_hobb;
    }
}
// The door, from beside it.
if (%slugmenace_stage >= ^slugmenace_shrine & %slugmenace_door_scanned = ^slugmenace_off) {
    if (~slugmenace_near_doors = true) {
        @slugmenace_scan_doors;
    }
    mes("You need to get closer to the doors for the scan to work.");
    return;
}
mes("The orb hums, finds nothing worth reporting, and goes quiet again.");

// The Mayor is the only npc in the quest worth scanning, and he is in a room of his own, so
// "is he within a few tiles" is the whole test. npc_findallzone walks the zone the player is in.
[proc,slugmenace_near_hobb]()(boolean)
def_int $found = 0;
npc_findallzone(coord);
while (npc_findnext = true) {
    if (npc_category = slugmenace_mayor) {
        $found = 1;
    }
}
if ($found = 1) {
    return(true);
}
return(false);

// The doors are 6 tiles wide and sit in a wall, so the test is a box rather than a tile.
[proc,slugmenace_near_doors]()(boolean)
if (coordz(coord) < ^slugmenace_doors_scan_z0 | coordz(coord) > ^slugmenace_doors_scan_z1) {
    return(false);
}
if (coordx(coord) < ^slugmenace_doors_scan_x0 | coordx(coord) > ^slugmenace_doors_scan_x1) {
    return(false);
}
return(true);

[label,slugmenace_scan_hobb]
mes("You turn the orb towards the Mayor. It goes cold in your hand.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,sad>That is not illness. There is something inside that man and it is using his mouth.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>I have seen a reading like that once before, in a report I was not supposed to read. Tell the colonel.");
// The same flag the door's scan sets. It is the quest's "Savant has a reading" bit, and the first
// thing she gets a reading of is the Mayor.
%slugmenace_door_scanned = ^slugmenace_on;

[label,slugmenace_scan_doors]
// ONE FREE SLOT, because the scan hands over an item. Old School checks this and says so, rather
// than taking the scan and dropping the transcription.
if (inv_freespace(inv) = 0) {
    ~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>I can copy those glyphs, but you have nowhere to put the copy. Empty a pocket and scan again.");
    return;
}
mes("You hold the orb up to the door. The glyphs crawl.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,quiz>I thought so. Those glyphs look similar to some ancient Saradomin runes I studied at the academy.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>Hmm. I know a man who can translate them for us. Just be careful - he is not a member of the Knights.");
inv_add(inv, slug_door_transcription, 1);
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>I have added a transcript of the runes into your pack.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>The man you need to see is called Jorral. You can find him at his outpost, north-west of Ardougne.");
~chatplayer("<p,happy>Fantastic - I'll get right on it.");
%slugmenace_door_scanned = ^slugmenace_on;
if (%slugmenace_stage < ^slugmenace_transcribed) {
    %slugmenace_stage = ^slugmenace_transcribed;
    ~send_quest_progress(questlist:slugmenace, %slugmenace_stage, ^slugmenace_complete);
}

// =========================================================================== Contact
[opheld2,slug_commorb]
switch_int (%slugmenace_stage) {
    case ^slugmenace_not_started :
        ~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>Nothing to report. Sir Tiffy has not given me anything to work on.");
    case ^slugmenace_briefed :
        ~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>Col. O'Niall is a retired Knight on the Witchaven dock. Say the phrase, however silly it sounds.");
    case ^slugmenace_asking :
        ~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>Hmm. Sounds like Witchaven has some problems at the moment.");
        ~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>The Mayor, the priest and the fisherman. Talk to all three, and scan the Mayor - I want a reading of whatever that is.");
    case ^slugmenace_shrine :
        ~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>The ruin west of the village. There is a wall down there that is not a wall - push it.");
    case ^slugmenace_transcribed : @slugmenace_contact_doors;
    case ^slugmenace_translated :
        ~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>Mother Mallum. Take that name back to the colonel and then to the priest.");
    case ^slugmenace_pages :
        ~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>Three pages. The Mayor's desk, Lovecraft's drawer, and whatever the colonel has been sitting on.");
    case ^slugmenace_runes :
        ~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>Five runes, five altars. Then the door, and bring something to hit it with.");
    case ^slugmenace_told :
        ~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,sad>Go and see Sir Tiffy. I am not putting what I just heard in a written report.");
    case default :
        ~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,happy>Savant out.");
}

[label,slugmenace_contact_doors]
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>What did you think of those doors? Spooky, hey?");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>Very. Though I can't shake the feeling that I've seen something like that before.");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>They did look really out of place. I wonder who put them there?");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>The answer is probably contained within those strange glyphs.");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>I only hope that Jorral can translate them.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>He has a very good track record in translating ancient runes.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>Although, to be fair, he does tend to get a bit obsessive at times.");
~chatplayer("<p,happy>Thanks for the warning, Savant.");

// =========================================================================== Playback
// The step the player is on, in one line, because the quest's instructions arrive by voice and
// there is otherwise no way to hear them twice.
[opheld4,slug_commorb]
switch_int (%slugmenace_stage) {
    case ^slugmenace_briefed : ~mesbox("...report to Col. O'Niall in Witchaven. In Falador, the geese fly backwards on Tuesdays...");
    case ^slugmenace_asking : ~mesbox("...the Mayor, Brother Maledict and Holgart the fisherman. And scan the Mayor...");
    case ^slugmenace_shrine : ~mesbox("...the old ruin west of the village. Look for a wall that isn't one...");
    case ^slugmenace_transcribed : ~mesbox("...the man you need to see is called Jorral. His outpost is north-west of Ardougne...");
    case ^slugmenace_translated : ~mesbox("...Mother Mallum. Take it to the colonel, and then to Brother Maledict...");
    case ^slugmenace_pages : ~mesbox("...three pages. The Mayor's desk, Lovecraft's drawer, and the colonel...");
    case ^slugmenace_runes : ~mesbox("...five runes, five altars. Air, water, earth, fire, mind...");
    case ^slugmenace_told : ~mesbox("...go and see Sir Tiffy...");
    case default : ~mesbox("The orb replays a long silence and then Savant saying 'is that thing still on?'.");
}

// =========================================================================== Jorral
// Making History declares [opnpc1,makinghistory_jorral]; this hooks in ahead of it. Jorral will
// talk about the transcription whether or not Making History has been started, which is what the
// quick guide means by its note about that quest - the two are independent.
[proc,slugmenace_jorral_wants]()(boolean)
if (%slugmenace_stage ! ^slugmenace_transcribed) {
    return(false);
}
return(true);

[label,slugmenace_jorral]
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>Excuse me?");
~chatnpc("<p,quiz>Yes, can I help you?");
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>I understand that you are something of a historian?");
~chatnpc("<p,laugh>Hah! I am the foremost historian in the world.");
~chatplayer("<p,happy>Great. I was wondering if you could translate something for me, please?");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Possibly. I am very busy, you see, and my services don't come cheap.");
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>Hmm. How much are we talking?");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Well, I am very busy, but I could fit you in sometime next month.");
~chatplayer("<p,sad>That was a bit longer than I was willing to wait. Can't you fit me in any sooner?");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>I'm afraid not. You see, I have this ongoing series of texts that need to be catalogued as soon as possible.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>Psst.");
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>Savant?");
~chatnpc("<p,quiz>What?");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,sad>Drat. I was hoping he wouldn't notice.");
~chatnpc("<p,quiz>Excuse me, but are you talking to your backpack?");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Um, no. Savant, help.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>Uh. Tell him that you're working for a wizard who's sending you telepathic instructions.");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>I, err, am working for a wizard who is giving me telepathic instructions.");
~chatnpc("<p,quiz>Riiiight. Okay. What does this, err, voice want you to do?");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>We have a front company who keeps Jorral on retainer.");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>We have a...");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,angry>No! Hang on, I wasn't finished.");
~chatplayer("<p,sad>Sorry.");
~chatnpc("<p,quiz>Pardon?");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Not you.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>Can I finish now? Anyway - tell him you are working for Petmel Books.");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Apparently I'm working for Petmel Books, and this document is from them.");
~chatnpc("<p,happy>Oh, right! That explains the mild insanity. No problem; hand over the document and I'll have a look.");
if (inv_total(inv, slug_door_transcription) = 0) {
    ~chatplayer("<p,sad>Um, I don't appear to have it on me.");
    ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Well, run along and fetch it then.");
    return;
}
~chatnpc("<p,quiz>Hmm. Interesting. Very interesting.");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>It's an early variation on a script used by the priests of Saradomin a long time ago.");
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>What does it say?");
~chatnpc("<p,happy>Look, you can see how the sentence structure and grammar evolved from the...");
~chatplayer("<p,angry>Yes, yes, I'm sure it's very interesting. But what does it say?");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Hmph. It seems this text pertains to a great battle between the temple of Saradomin and something called the Mahey'ish Medron.");
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>The Mavis Merton?");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Mahey'ish Medron. I think it's a corruption of an even earlier language, and actually refers to something called Mother Mallum.");
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>And?");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Well, there isn't a whole lot more. They managed to trap the Mother Mallum behind a mystical prison, where she was to wait for all time.");
~chatplayer("<p,happy>Well, thanks for that. You have been a great help.");
~chatnpc("<p,laugh>Any time. I recommend a doctor for those voices, though.");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Uh, right. Goodbye.");
%slugmenace_stage = ^slugmenace_translated;
%slugmenace_translated = ^slugmenace_on;
// The village turns here. The player now knows what is in it, and 474 brings the second form of
// each villager in across these stages - see slugmenace.varbit for why all three go together.
%slugmenace_villagers_turned = ^slugmenace_on;
~send_quest_progress(questlist:slugmenace, %slugmenace_stage, ^slugmenace_complete);
~slugmenace_jorral_debrief;

// Savant's own history lesson, immediately afterwards. It is the quest's only exposition and it
// is where "repair the prison" comes from, so it is not optional and not behind a Contact.
[proc,slugmenace_jorral_debrief]()
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,happy>Come in. This is Savant. That was the final piece of the puzzle I needed.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>I've cross-referenced the name Mahey'ish Medron with some other texts and been able to piece together some of the history.");
~chatplayer("<p,happy>Finally, some solid information.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>It seems this isn't the first time the Temple Knights have run across this Mother Mallum character.");
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Now, why doesn't that surprise me?");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,sad>Centuries ago we discovered that a great evil had taken control of some of the most influential people in the world. That great evil was the Mother Mallum.");
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>So what happened?");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>It took the few remaining uncorrupted knights all their wit and strength to devise a method of removing sea slug possession.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,sad>Once freed, the Knights pursued a great crusade to destroy her. She was too powerful, and the best they could do was trap her inside a mystical prison.");
~chatplayer("<p,sad>It looks like she's breaking free of that prison.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>Right. The best thing we can do is repair or reinforce it before she escapes.");
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>Did your research reveal how she was trapped in the first place?");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,sad>No. I hit a brick wall after that. We had a dragon crash land on our headquarters a few years ago, and the fire destroyed a lot of our records.");
~chatplayer("<p,sad>Drat. That complicates things.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,neutral>I think the best thing you can do is take a look around Witchaven. Speak to some of the locals and see if there are any clues to be found.");
~chatplayer("<p,happy>Righty ho. I'll get to it. Thanks, Savant.");
~chatnpc_specific("Savant", wanted_savant, "<p,happy>Don't mention it. Savant out.");
